# Project foundations

- Use strict TypeScript; avoid `any`, unsafe casts, non-null assertions, dead code, and speculative abstractions.
- Offline-first personal finance: SQLite + MMKV only — no backend, telemetry, or fake API URLs.
- Use theme tokens and shared design primitives instead of hardcoded visual values in feature UI.
- Organize product code under `src/features/<feature>/` with thin `screens/`, local `components/`, and `hooks/`. Keep pure logic in `src/domain/` and persistence in `src/db/`.
- Prefer local React state; Zustand for shared UI prefs only. Do not invent unrelated routes or placeholders.
- Use npm commands. Run `npm run verify` after substantive changes.
- Do not edit lockfiles, generated native resources, or build output unless explicitly requested.
- Never commit or push — this repo stays local-only (see `local-only-git.mdc`).
